---
type: readme
title: README for the visitedlink core directory
summary: Explains that this directory holds visitedlink types without //content dependencies so they can be used in iOS codepaths such as HistoryService without layering errors.
---

This directory exists for "core" types within visitedlink, which do not include
any dependencies on //content. As a result, classes in this directory can be
accessed in codepaths used in ios-builds, i.e. HistoryService, without
encountering layering errors.
